From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Project Luma <builds@project-luma.local>
Date: Thu, 17 Sep 2026 15:10:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] luma: the unread badge takes the deeper Ember

White on the Ember the badge shipped with, #f26a1b, measures 3.06:1, below
the 4.5:1 WCAG AA asks for text at 9.5px. The owner chose the deeper Ember
(2026-09-17): #c24a0b, which measures 4.91:1 with white and still reads as
Ember beside the rest of the system.

Only the one fill constant changes. Size, placement, the cap, the dot, the
ring and the pop are the same, and the ring still takes the shelf's own
surface colour. tests/gnome-shell/dock-badges.js now computes the contrast
of BADGE_INK on BADGE_FILL and fails below 4.5:1, so the next change to
either colour has to keep the count legible.

Generated against the Shell .103 tree with 0145–0147 applied, for release
.106.
---
diff --git a/js/ui/lumaDockBadgeModel.js b/js/ui/lumaDockBadgeModel.js
index 3e4859f..9d9f487 100644
--- a/js/ui/lumaDockBadgeModel.js
+++ b/js/ui/lumaDockBadgeModel.js
@@ -4,10 +4,11 @@
 // No GI imports, so the rules can be checked with plain gjs at build time
 // (tests/gnome-shell/dock-badges.js). lumaDockBadges.js draws them.
 
-// The badge's fill and ink. Ember was chosen by eye from three styles; white on
-// #f26a1b measures about 3.1:1. If the owner darkens it for contrast, this is
-// the one place to change.
-export const BADGE_FILL = '#f26a1b';
+// The badge's fill and ink, in one place. The owner chose Ember by eye from
+// three styles, then took the deeper Ember (2026-09-17) so the count meets
+// WCAG AA: white on #c24a0b measures 4.91:1, where the original #f26a1b
+// measured 3.06:1 and failed at 9.5px.
+export const BADGE_FILL = '#c24a0b';
 export const BADGE_INK = '#ffffff';
 
 // Interim product defaults, each one line to flip.
